# Shared surfaces (#231): a change to any path matched here takes a diff out of
# the quick flow at close, whatever its size — these are the seams other repos,
# issues and gates read, where a small edit has a large blast radius.
#
# One pattern per line: a path.Match glob (`*` does not cross `/`), or a
# directory with a trailing `/`, meaning anything under it. This file itself is
# always a shared surface, and close reads it as committed at the review window's
# base AND head, so a branch cannot loosen its own shell. `sdlc change-code
# --help` prints the rest of the shell.

# The vocabulary models and their Go embedding — every consumer derives from them.
construct/vocabulary/*.cue
pkg/vocab/

# The base layer propagated to every downstream repo.
construct/base.manifest
AGENTS.base.md

# What the judges are told: the ARCH registry and the boundary-review procedure.
cmd/sdlc/internal/judge/architecture.md
cmd/sdlc/internal/judge/code-review.md

# Persisted gate state and the calibration ledger schema.
cmd/sdlc/internal/gatestate/
cmd/sdlc/internal/estimate/ledger.go
